# Inventory Domain

## Entities

| Model | Role |
|-------|------|
| `Inventory` | Stock item (sku, levels, cost, expiry, supplier) |
| `Supplier` | Vendor + performance |
| `Purchase` / `PurchaseItem` | PO + line items; receive flow updates stock |
| `Waste` | Loss records; usually deducts stock |
| `StockTransaction` | Audit trail for every stock movement |

## Invariants

1. **Never change `current_stock` without a `StockTransaction`** (adjust, receive, waste, order deduct).
2. Order creation should deduct recipe ingredient stock and log transactions.
3. Purchase `receive-items` / status transitions must update inventory consistently.
4. Alerts: low stock (`current <= min`), out of stock (`<= 0`), expiring (near `expiry_date`).

## API surface (keep in sync with `js/api.js` / inventory module)

- `PATCH /api/inventory/{id}/adjust-stock`
- `GET /api/inventory/alerts/low-stock|expiring`
- `GET /api/inventory/{id}/transactions`
- Purchases: `PATCH .../status`, `POST .../receive-items`
- Waste + supplier performance/report endpoints under `/api/reports/*`

## Frontend

Inventory UI lives under inventory tab flags in Alpine state (`inventoryTab`: inventory, purchases, suppliers, waste, reports). Keep modular logic in `js/inventory.js`.
